# The ledger of `containers/deque`: the double-ended queue, what Go 1.27's
# `container/ring`, Rust 1.100's `VecDeque` and Python 3.15's
# `collections.deque` offer, one block per capability, and what Heroes
# answers to each; and the list of links, Go's `container/list` and Rust's
# `LinkedList`, which stands pending here, its two ends being the deque's.
#
# A record takes no type parameter, so a deque is a shape beside the
# program's own item list, lent with `@`; no list shortens in place, so the
# ring keeps a count and reuses its list's room.

## The double-ended queue

capability deque/make  an empty double-ended queue, or one over a list held
  heroes  deque.new, deque.over
  go      ring.New
  rust    VecDeque::new, VecDeque::default, VecDeque::from, VecDeque::from_iter, VecDeque::try_with_capacity
  python  collections.deque, deque.copy, deque.__copy__
  note    a ring over the program's item list that doubles when full and is cut back when three quarters stand empty; Go's `ring.New(n)` makes n links holding nothing, which with no `nil` here is `new_bounded_deque(n)`, the use it is put to. A copy is `=` of the shape and the list

capability deque/bounded  a deque that holds at most a number of items, the oldest dropped
  heroes  deque.new_bounded, deque.capacity
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  deque.maxlen
  note    Python's: a push at one end of a full deque drops the item at the other, observed (`maxlen=3` after a to e gives c d e, then `appendleft("z")` gives z c d); an insert into a full one is refused `invalid`, as Python raises

capability deque/push  an item added at either end
  heroes  deque.push_back, deque.push_front
  go      -
  rust    VecDeque::push_back, VecDeque::push_front, VecDeque::push_back_mut, VecDeque::push_front_mut, VecDeque::extend, VecDeque::extend_front, VecDeque::extend_one, VecDeque::append, VecDeque::prepend
  python  deque.append, deque.appendleft, deque.extend, deque.extendleft, deque.__iadd__
  note    many items are a loop; Python's `extendleft` reverses them, which a loop of `deque.push_front` does too

capability deque/pop  an item taken from either end
  heroes  deque.pop_back, deque.pop_front
  go      -
  rust    VecDeque::pop_back, VecDeque::pop_front, VecDeque::pop_back_if, VecDeque::pop_front_if
  python  deque.pop, deque.popleft
  note    an empty deque is `not_found`, where Python raises IndexError and Rust answers None; the slot freed takes a copy of a live item, so the item popped is let go at once. Rust's `pop_if` is `deque.first` asked first

capability deque/ends  the item at either end, left in
  heroes  deque.first, deque.last
  go      -
  rust    VecDeque::front, VecDeque::back, VecDeque::front_mut, VecDeque::back_mut
  python  -
  note    Python reads `d[0]` and `d[-1]`, which abort here past the ends where these answer `not_found`

capability deque/index  an item read or written by its place from the front
  heroes  deque.get, deque.put
  go      ring.Next, ring.Prev, ring.Move
  rust    VecDeque::get, VecDeque::get_mut, VecDeque::index, VecDeque::index_mut, VecDeque::swap
  python  deque.__getitem__, deque.__setitem__
  note    a place is from 0 and never below it, where Python counts from the end with a negative one; Go's `Move(n)` is a place n further, and a swap two reads and two writes. `get` is the checked reader, failing `not_found` past the ends; `put` past them aborts, as Rust's `index_mut` and an index past a list's end do (the coherence review's D09, 2026-11-21)

capability deque/insert-remove  an item put at or taken from a place inside
  heroes  deque.insert, deque.remove_at
  go      ring.Link, ring.Unlink
  rust    VecDeque::insert, VecDeque::insert_mut, VecDeque::remove, VecDeque::swap_remove_back, VecDeque::swap_remove_front
  python  deque.insert, deque.__delitem__, deque.remove
  note    each moves the items on the nearer side, at most half; Rust's swap removes are `deque.get` of the end, `deque.put` over the place and a pop. Go's `Link` and `Unlink` splice links of two rings, which is items put in or taken out at a place here. Python's `remove` by value is `lists.index_of` over `deque.to_list`, then this. A place outside the deque aborts, as Rust's `insert` and `remove` past the end do; a full bounded deque is `insert`'s one failure (D09)

capability deque/rotate  the items turned round
  heroes  deque.rotate_left, deque.rotate_right
  go      ring.Move
  rust    VecDeque::rotate_left, VecDeque::rotate_right
  python  deque.rotate
  note    Python's `rotate(1)` gives [4, 1, 2, 3] of [1, 2, 3, 4], observed, which is `deque.rotate_right` by 1; a full item list turns by moving its head alone

capability deque/to-list  the items front to back as a list
  heroes  deque.to_list
  go      ring.Do
  rust    VecDeque::iter, VecDeque::iter_mut, VecDeque::into_iter, VecDeque::as_slices, VecDeque::as_mut_slices, VecDeque::make_contiguous, VecDeque::range, VecDeque::range_mut, VecDeque::drain, vec_deque::Iter, vec_deque::IterMut, vec_deque::IntoIter, vec_deque::Drain
  python  deque.__iter__, deque.__reversed__
  note    a walk is a `for` over this list; Go's `Do` calls a function at each link, which is that walk

capability deque/size  how many items a deque holds
  heroes  deque.size
  go      ring.Len
  rust    VecDeque::len, VecDeque::is_empty
  python  deque.__len__
  note    -

capability deque/clear  a deque emptied or cut
  heroes  deque.clear
  go      -
  rust    VecDeque::clear, VecDeque::truncate, VecDeque::truncate_to_range
  python  deque.clear
  note    a cut to a length is pops from the back until it is reached

capability deque/search-and-reshape  a deque searched, counted, reversed, sorted, filtered or resized
  heroes  deque.to_list
  go      -
  rust    VecDeque::contains, VecDeque::binary_search, VecDeque::binary_search_by, VecDeque::binary_search_by_key, VecDeque::partition_point, VecDeque::retain, VecDeque::retain_mut, VecDeque::retain_back, VecDeque::extract_if, VecDeque::resize, VecDeque::resize_with, VecDeque::split_off, VecDeque::splice, VecDeque::extend_from_within, VecDeque::prepend_from_within, vec_deque::Splice, vec_deque::ExtractIf
  python  deque.count, deque.index, deque.reverse, deque.__contains__, deque.__add__, deque.__mul__, deque.__imul__
  note    the items as a list, worked on by `lists` (`lists.contains`, `lists.binary_search`, `lists.reverse`, `lists.remove_where`, `lists.resize`, `lists.cycle`) and given back by `deque.over`: each is linear in the size in Rust and Python too

## The list of links

capability links/list  a list of links: an item put or taken at a handle held, or moved to either end, in constant time
  heroes  pending
  go      list.New, list.List.Init, list.List.Len, list.List.Front, list.List.Back, list.List.PushFront, list.List.PushBack, list.List.PushFrontList, list.List.PushBackList, list.List.InsertBefore, list.List.InsertAfter, list.List.MoveToFront, list.List.MoveToBack, list.List.MoveBefore, list.List.MoveAfter, list.List.Remove, list.Element.Next, list.Element.Prev
  rust    LinkedList::new, LinkedList::default, LinkedList::push_front, LinkedList::push_back, LinkedList::push_front_mut, LinkedList::push_back_mut, LinkedList::pop_front, LinkedList::pop_back, LinkedList::front, LinkedList::back, LinkedList::front_mut, LinkedList::back_mut, LinkedList::len, LinkedList::is_empty, LinkedList::clear, LinkedList::contains, LinkedList::append, LinkedList::split_off, LinkedList::remove, LinkedList::retain, LinkedList::extract_if, LinkedList::iter, LinkedList::iter_mut, LinkedList::into_iter, LinkedList::cursor_front, LinkedList::cursor_back, LinkedList::cursor_front_mut, LinkedList::cursor_back_mut, LinkedList::extend, LinkedList::extend_one, LinkedList::from, LinkedList::from_iter, linked_list::Cursor, linked_list::CursorMut, linked_list::Iter, linked_list::IterMut, linked_list::IntoIter, linked_list::ExtractIf
  python  -
  note    the cache's two lists of links are this inside; a public one needs handles that outlive a removal, slots kept stable by a free list rather than the dense slots every structure here keeps, and is not written yet. Both ends are the deque's, and a key moved to either end the indexed map's

dropped capacity  room asked ahead of the items: every structure here grows by itself and gives room back when three quarters stand empty
